# COMMISSION — Design how {{SYSTEM}} gets specified to the SDD set

**For:** one fresh session with this repository connected
**Subject:** the plan by which what has been carried in becomes the {{THINGS}} things `SDD-01`
names, for the whole of {{SYSTEM}}
**Standing:** this commission designs a run. **It does not perform it, and it writes no
specification.** Read it whole before your first act.
**Raised:** {{DATE}} · scaffolded by `kit spec new {{SYSTEM_ID}}`

---

## 0. What you produce, in one sentence

**One machine-readable plan, its renderer, and the page it renders** — saying, for each of
the {{THINGS}} things `SDD-01` names, what the carried material gives towards it, what must be
written from nothing, in what order, by whom, at what cost, and **what tells the person
doing it that they got it wrong.**

**You author no requirement, no record, no use case, no screen and no model.** Things are
counted, not written. A page that contains one specified record has exceeded this
commission.

---

## 1. Why this run exists, and what it is really for

`SDD-01` §16: *no document produced so far carries a conformance claim made rule by rule.*
The standards have been designed, drafted, built and made consistent. **Using them is a
different act from writing them, and it is the act that has not happened.**

So the purpose of the run you are designing is **not the specification.** It is the list of
places where a standard could not be followed, was ambiguous, cost more than it was worth,
or turned out to be silent — **recorded with the moment it happened, from the first sitting
onward.** Your plan must carry the register that collects it as a standing obligation of
every piece of work, never as a closing step. **A plan that puts the amendment register at
the end has misunderstood the run.**

